## Tutorials

Strings are used for storing text/characters.

For example, "Hello World" is a string.

Astringvariable contains a collection of characters surrounded by double quotes (""):

To use strings, you must include an additional header file in the source 
code, the<string>library:

Note:Strings can contain multiple words, spaces, and punctuation:

### Code Examples

```
string greeting = "Hello";

---

// Include the string library
#include <string>
// Create a string variable
string greeting = "Hello";
// Print the string
cout << greeting;

---

string greeting = "Hello and welcome!";
cout << greeting;
```

